# StockSense — complete environment variable reference.
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development, and set the same variables
# (minus the dev-only ones) on your hosting provider. See DEPLOY.md.
#
# Every variable the app reads is listed here (grep `process.env` in app/,
# vite.config.ts to verify). No real credentials are needed to run tests,
# lint, typecheck, or the production build.

# ── Shopify app credentials (REQUIRED for auth; from Partner Dashboard) ──────
# Partner Dashboard → Apps → your app → "Client ID" (this is SHOPIFY_API_KEY)
# and "Client secret" (this is SHOPIFY_API_SECRET). Never commit real values.
SHOPIFY_API_KEY=replace-with-your-api-key
SHOPIFY_API_SECRET=replace-with-your-api-secret

# ── Access scopes (REQUIRED) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must match [access_scopes] in shopify.app.toml exactly. Comma-separated.
SCOPES=read_inventory,read_products,read_orders,read_locations,write_inventory

# ── Base URL (REQUIRED) — the ONE env var that drives everything ─────────────
# The public HTTPS URL of the deployed app, e.g. https://stocksense.onrender.com
# (no trailing slash). Used for OAuth, billing return URLs, and it is the base
# for the privacy policy / terms URLs (app/lib/config.ts derives
# ${SHOPIFY_APP_URL}/privacy-policy.html and ${SHOPIFY_APP_URL}/terms.html).
# In local dev, `shopify app dev` sets this to your tunnel URL automatically.
SHOPIFY_APP_URL=https://your-app.example.com

# ── Database (REQUIRED) — Postgres, e.g. Supabase free tier ────────────────
# Use the Supabase *session pooler* connection string (port 5432, IPv4 —
# Render can't reach Supabase's IPv6-only direct host) and keep tables in their
# own schema so Supabase's Data API never exposes them:
#   postgresql://<role>.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-<n>-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?schema=stocksense
# Migrations run on boot (`npm run setup` → prisma migrate deploy).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/postgres?schema=stocksense

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Custom shop domains (comma-separated) to allow in OAuth, e.g.
# "example.com,www.example.com". Only needed if merchants use custom domains.
# SHOP_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=

# Billing test mode. Shopify test charges never take real money (required on
# development/test shops). Leave unset: the app uses test charges unless
# NODE_ENV=production, where it charges for real. Override explicitly if needed:
#   SHOPIFY_BILLING_TEST=true   # force test charges (e.g. staging on prod infra)
#   SHOPIFY_BILLING_TEST=false  # force real charges
# SHOPIFY_BILLING_TEST=

# ── Dev-only (set by `shopify app dev` / vite; ignore on hosts) ─────────────
# HOST: tunnel host passed by the Shopify CLI (vite.config.ts maps it to
# SHOPIFY_APP_URL). FRONTEND_PORT: HMR port for the dev server.
# PORT: HTTP port for the dev server (default 3000); remix-serve also reads it.
# HOST=
# FRONTEND_PORT=8002
# PORT=3000

# ── Runtime (set by the host; do not set locally) ────────────────────────────
# NODE_ENV=production   # set by Render/Fly/Docker; keeps Prisma client global